<tr><td colspan=4><font size=2 face=verdana color=#ffffff>It had been a long ride... Espirius woke up to find himself half-naked and starving in a large grass field that seemed to stretch for miles on end. He picked himself up and dusted himself off to get a better look around. He wasn't quite exactly sure where he was.. nor did he remember how he got there, but there was a large welt on his forehead, which appeared to be the source of the headache he now realized he was having.... magically induced.
<p>
Espirius stumbled to his feet and tried to walk across the clearing, realizing that his strength was also sapped out of him, tried to keep his balance and collapsed on the ground. It was started to come back to him.. a battle, of some sort.. one of which he was grossly outmatched, now feeling the paranoia and frustration turn his stomach. Kokoro! He had just found her when... when....
<p> 
... he can't remember what happened next... he mused to himself that that was the will of the caster who teleported him to where he lay now, perhaps some sort of cruel punishment, insult on top of injury. Realizing he had no more strength of his own, he called out for help as he could see the sun setting in the distance. 
<p> 
It hadn't been much time when Espirius heard footsteps behind him, though he saw no one there. He counted this to being delirious as now he was beginning to shake uncontrollably from hunger, magic, fear, or a combination of the three.
When he turned around again, there was a man standing there, nearly about 6 feet away or so.. just enough to be comfortably out of reach.
<p>
The man stood nearly six feet tall and was very well built. He had a intricate longbow slung across his back. His face told a story of his personality, a full beard and mustache complimented a set of piercing eyes that Espirius knew could view your soul if needed be. The man looked down on Espirius for a moment and his expression lifted and turned to a smile.

"Hail friend! " he said as he knelt down, still not approaching him."Got yourself into a bind?" he asked.
Espirius stopped himself shaking for a moment to reply "Yessir... I...", he shook his head as a wave of lighheadedness made itself known to him. He had to fight to remain conscious.
The man stood up and walked over to him, and finally presented himself with an outstretched hand, "You look like you could use a bed and a good meal. I have some friends living nearby who can fix ya right up. My name is Hager Sureshot, I am a ranger of Surefall Glade. And you are..?"
Espirius smiled and reached out his hand, and would have returned the polite gesture, but as he did so, he could not stave off the second wave of vertigo mixed with nausea this time... and promptly passed out. 

